# @DISPLAY@

Independent Rust/Axum/SQLite and React/TypeScript application. You own its source and
may change its initial choices. No original starter checkout, shared runtime or
upstream synchronization is required. Authentication, authorization, sessions and
CSRF defenses are absent: this is a foundation preview, not a production guarantee.

## First day

1. Inspect the map below and [initialize your own Git repository](CONTRIBUTING.md#1-own-your-repository).
2. Choose Docker for the complete application, or native development for editing.
3. Follow [backend/frontend examples, tests and migrations](CONTRIBUTING.md).
4. Use [MAINTENANCE.md](MAINTENANCE.md), [security](SECURITY.md), and
   [release/recovery procedures](MAINTENANCE.md#releases-updates-and-recovery) before updates.

Generation does not initialize Git or copy source Git history. GitHub is optional;
use any host, adapting `.github/workflows` if your provider differs.

